 "notes": "94 WBADB rows within 2 km. Rows with no pool/pit/grave: S3295, S3212, S3321, S3162, S3365, S3315, E515, E513, E549, S3190, S3155, S3375, S3072. Not coded: 'complex water system' and bathhouse at S3251/E546 (no pool or cistern named), conduits, quarries, cupmarks, ossuaries as finds (S3235 workshop). Own-row 'shaft and other tombs' split into shaft tombs (cavity) and other tombs (kind unstated). Sheikh's tomb, 'Tombs' and 'burial complex' coded cavity false (kind not stated). Dating: where a row lists only the one feature (with finds or rock cuttings), it is treated as the feature's own row (D/L by row periods); otherwise component U. Excavation rows (E...) that repeat a survey row are coded again under their own id."
